A||||7||theogre||Cave Update||||6||
Z||000000||theogre||11-12-2001||02:40 PM||||The cave has been updated again...<P>Brakes... Thanks to Bruce at FTF Engineering, I now have the info about the solid faced rear pistons.<P>Fans... I've added notes for converting from the very expensive relay module used by the 2 speed fan to two standard GM fan relays.<P>Window Service... I added the stuff I do when windows are hard to crank or the motors are slow...<P>Comming soon:<P>Stick... Some general stuff from when I used to deal with allot of hydraulic clutches. It's not Fiero specific but it may at least give you some ideas to help bleeding and flushing.<P>Suspension... I've also got an article about changing struts comming. BTW, If you need struts... Check Pep Boys... I recently got front shocks and rear struts, Gabriel Pro Ryder Gas with "VST", for a little over $100us. I'm not sure if I just hit a sale that day or what but it was the lowest price for name branded stuff I could find. (Gabriel is made in U.S.A. for those of you that prefer that.)<P>Other Changes:<P>The Fiero Cave is increasing the use of Java Scripting. (This means WebTV will probably have more problems.) Child pages now have "true" back buttons on the bottom that return you to where you came from. (The three small pages that link off the brake service page... Others will use it in future.)<P>I've dropped all support for IE channels. No-one seems to be using it anyway... The channel page is there but won't be updated. I can't remember the last time the IE channel was updated. It will be likely dropped the next time I change the main page.<P>Q... Does anyone on the planet actually use the Content Advisor functions of IE or it's equivalent in other browsers? Web filters like Net Nanny?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||6
